  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Institutional Strengthening for Integrated Planning (ISIP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Data-driven and evidence-based planning are essential to ensure the effectiveness of policy implementation. UNDP Timor-Leste has committed to providing technical hands-on support on data-driven and evidence-based planning to the Government of Timor-Leste to strengthen the government&#x2019;s capacity in its planning and coordination. The support is given through three components, which are High Frequency (HiFy) phone-based survey, national census, and voluntary national review (VNR) on the implementation of SDGs. HiFy Survey and National Census are essential in providing the actual data of the country&#x2019;s situational analysis to be used as a background in delivering different initiatives by policymakers and development actors. The VNR component is critical to analyse the implementation of SDGs to be further adjusted and implemented by the government through its line ministries and bodies.</narrative>
  </description>
